{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And all the wells, etc.</b> Scripture placed this announcement adjacent to ״וַיְקַנְאוּ״ [and they envied him], etc., to say that the tribe of the wicked will not rest content with the lot of the righteous. And it informed us that they envied him, and further informed us that even toward Abraham they had borne envy and hatred — ״וְכָל הַבְּאֵרוֹת אֲשֶׁר״ [and all the wells which], etc. And its saying <b>they stopped them up and filled them with earth</b>, and it did not suffice to say merely 'they filled them with earth' — perhaps it is because after Abraham's death they specifically stopped them up: they placed stones at their mouths and did not abolish them entirely. But after the envy they bore toward Isaac, they added further wickedness in their envy and filled them with earth, so that they were as though they had never been. And for this reason Isaac needed to dig them anew, as it says in the adjacent verse: ״וַיַּחְפֹּר אֶת בְּאֵרֹת״ [and he dug the wells], etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:32.286764098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}